  message: "DONE. PR #1117, merged c9652b836e.\n\nTHE ACCEPTANCE TEST THIS ROW SET ITSELF, re-run on the merged tree rather than carried from the PR:\n  len(LEGACY_VALUE_PARSERS)        -> 8   (was 9 at ADR-0058's declaration)\n  py.py still in the closed set?   -> False\n  find_undeclared_value_parsers(.) -> []\n  _extract_return_type_name in py.py -> 0 occurrences (deleted)\n  py.py:395  reads  (symbol.meta or {}).get(\"return_type\")\n  py.py:3157 / :3273 stamp meta[\"return_type\"] = ast.unparse(...) at both emit sites\nThe set shrinking is the point: it distinguishes a migration from a declaration.\n\nTHE ROW'S OWN PRESCRIBED FIX WAS WRONG, and I wrote it. It said \"populate FileAnalysis.method_return_types and FileAnalysis.class_field_types from py.py's Pass 1\". py.py has its OWN `FileAnalysis` (py.py:2181) -- a different dataclass from the tree-sitter base's, carrying NEITHER field -- and, decisively, it never reaches the core linker that needs the same fact. The home that travels is `Symbol.meta[\"return_type\"]`: a registered meta key (axis_meta_keys.py:1082) that java, luau and apex already populate, and whose sibling `inferred_return_type` names Python as an intended producer. ADR-0058's table is amended in place to say so, because it would have sent the next reader the same wrong way. I derived that fix yesterday from the ADR without checking the class -- rule 2, on my own row.\n\nEQUIVALENCE MEASURED BEFORE WRITING CODE: over 33,740 functions in this repository the AST-derived return type and the signature parse I was about to retire agreed on EVERY one, 0 disagreements. It holds because WI-hopiz made display-mode truncation preserve the return type rather than cut it off. So this is a structural move, not a behaviour change.\n\nSPLIT OF RESPONSIBILITY: the producer records the declared type VERBATIM (`Optional[Foo]` included); the narrowness -- simple identifiers only -- stays the consumer's policy. Neither widened nor narrowed, and both halves are pinned by tests, including a DIFFERENCE arm that renders every signature without its return type and shows the inference is unaffected.\n\nSURVEY DIFF (fihun_after -> ribak_after):\n  method-call-recovery edges   62 -> 62, IDENTICAL set (0 lost, 0 gained)\n  receiver_type_hint          809 -> 810 (0 lost)\n  meta[\"return_type\"]           4 -> 31,932\n  resolved calls, span-insensitive: 119,591 -> 119,710, 3 lost -- and all 3 are the\n    deleted function's own edges (its call site, plus rsplit and isidentifier)\n\nA MEASUREMENT TRAP WORTH THE NEXT READER'S TIME: the FIRST diff read 1,075 resolved-call losses, which looks like a serious regression. They were py.py symbols whose line SPANS shifted because this change adds ~30 lines above them, churning their ids. Comparing span-insensitively gives 3. An id that embeds a span is not a stable key across an edit to the same file.\n\nVERIFICATION: full affected slice 22,214 passed / 0 failed -- including four files the REGENERATED manifest newly selected (BRANCHES_test_python_ast_analysis.py among them) that the pre-change chunk split did not cover; a green run on the stale split would have looked complete. mypy strict ratchet 667 = baseline. Ruff clean. All 18 pre-commit gates. Every added line covered.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM.\n  - class_field_types is STILL unwritten by python. This row moved the RETURN TYPE only, which is the fact py.py:5881 parsed. The value_type half belongs to method_call_recovery.py:209, a core linker, and there is NO registered meta key for a field's declared type -- declaring one is ADR-0024 creation practice and a separate argument.\n  - The remaining EIGHT parsers are untouched: csharp x2, kotlin x2, js_ts, dart, jackson_dispatch, method_call_recovery. Each is its own language's arm and files on its own evidence.\n  - Recall on OTHER repositories was not measured. One python-heavy corpus."  # a5ad
